Book Store Order Analysis (SQL Project)
Project Overview
This project performs an end-to-end data analysis for an online book store using SQL. 
By querying inventory, sales, customer demographics, and order data, the project extracts key business metrics and performance insights to optimize inventory management and 
track revenue trends. 

Database Schema
The database book_store consists of three core tables: 
books: Contains book details (book_id, title, author, genre, price, stock, published_year). 
customers: Holds customer demographical info (customer_id, name, city, country). 
orders: Tracks transaction records (order_id, customer_id, book_id, quantity, total_amount, order_date). 
Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)
Total Inventory Stock: 25,056 units 
Total Books Cataloged: 500 titles 
Total Revenue Generated: ₹7,56,629 
Total Books Sold: 2,697 units 
Total Unique Genres: 7 categories
Customer Geographic Reach: Customers across 489 distinct cities

Key Business Takeaways
1. Low Stock Management:Identified 251 book titles with stock under 50 units, signaling a need for inventory replenishment.
2. Customer Demographics:Highly distributed customer base across 489 cities, enabling localized marketing efforts.
3. Revenue Distribution:Successfully calculated lifetime customer value to target high-value clients and tracked remaining stock post-fulfillment.
